<title>UK: SOCCER-SCOTLAND CALL UP UNCAPPED WEIR.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-SCOTLAND CALL UP UNCAPPED WEIR.</headline>
<dateline>GLASGOW 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scotland manager Craig Brown</p>
<p>named a 21-man squad on Friday for his country's next three</p>
<p>matches.</p>
<p>Scotland play Wales in a friendly on May 27, Malta in a</p>
<p>friendly on June 1 and a World Cup qualifier against Belarus in</p>
<p>Minsk on June 8.</p>
<p>Brown has called up uncapped David Weir after a series of</p>
<p>fine performances for Hearts this season but the defence has an</p>
<p>experimental look about it because of the absences of regulars</p>
<p>like Colin Calderwood and Colin Hendry through suspension and</p>
<p>injury.</p>
<p>Squad:</p>
<p>Goalkeepers: Jim Leighton (Hibernian), Neil Sullivan</p>
<p>(Wimbledon), Scott Howie (Motherwell)</p>
<p>Defenders: Tommy Boyd (Celtic), Craig Burley (Chelsea), David</p>
<p>Weir (Hearts), Brian McAllister, Tosh McKinlay (Celtic), Jack McNamara (Celtic), Derek Whyte (Middlesbrough)</p>
<p>Midfielders: Christian Dailly (Derby),  Kevin Gallacher</p>
<p>(Blackburn), Scott Gemmill (Nottingham Forest), Paul Lambert</p>
<p>(Borussia Dortmund), Gary McAllister (Coventry),</p>
<p>Forwards: John Collins (Monaco), Gordon Durie (Rangers),</p>
<p>Darren Jackson (Hibernian), Ally McCoist (Rangers), John Spencer</p>
<p>(Queens Park Rangers), Billy Dodds (Aberdeen).</p>
